**Tool steps — not executable in this session.** `search_public_recipes`, `plan_event`, `validate_program`, `analyze_schedule` and `visualize_schedule` are unavailable here, so I can neither confirm a catalog match (step 1) nor return a live URL or Gantt (steps 4–6), and I will not invent either. Had they been available I would have: run `search_public_recipes` first for "product launch" and stopped if a match returned a timeline; otherwise run `validate_program` on the JSON above and fix every reported error; then `analyze_schedule` with `finishAt: "21:00"` — expecting `startAt ≈ 17:03`, makespan ≈ 3h57m, critical path `av-line-check → av-booth/strike-stage` (the stage-strike tail, not the program), and `bindingConstraints` naming `stage` (contended 17:00–17:50 and again 20:27–20:57) rather than the clock; then `visualize_schedule` to publish the shareable timeline and quote its ASCII Gantt and wall-clock itinerary verbatim.

Two flags on the JSON itself, in the interest of not overclaiming: `doors-open` and `bar-reopen` are 0-second milestones, so if the validator rejects a zero-second `fixed` duration, fold each one into the `startTrigger` of the step that follows it and the schedule is unchanged. And `ceo-keynote` is declared on `stage` only — the projector is physically held by the deck during the keynote, but a step carries one `task`, and nothing else claims the projector in that window, so the constraint set is still correct.
